Package: sermo-core-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: sermo dialog engine - static core library and headers
 sermo builds native windows from an XML description, so that a shell script
 can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge. It succeeds
 gtkdialog and keeps its XML language. One hardened core parses the description
 and runs the actions; each backend draws it with one toolkit.
 .
 This package contains the core, libsermocore, as a static library, with its
 headers and its pkg-config file, for building a backend. It uses no graphical
 toolkit. The backends packaged here already embed the core and do not need it.

Package: sermo-backend-gtk3
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: sermo-backend
Breaks: gtk3sermo (<< 2.0~)
Replaces: gtk3sermo (<< 2.0~)
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - GTK 3 backend
 sermo builds native windows from an XML description, so that a shell script
 can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge. It succeeds
 gtkdialog and keeps its XML language. One hardened core parses the description
 and runs the actions; each backend draws it with one toolkit.
 .
 This package provides gtk3sermo, the GTK 3 backend, the reference port of
 sermo. It also offers the sermo command through update-alternatives.

