Package: sermo-backend-lvgl
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: sermo-backend
Conflicts: sermo-backend-lvgl-leger
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - LVGL backend
 sermo builds native windows from an XML description, so that a shell script
 can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge. It succeeds
 gtkdialog and keeps its XML language. One hardened core parses the description
 and runs the actions; each backend draws it with one toolkit.
 .
 This package provides lvglsermo, the backend for kiosks and embedded screens,
 drawn with LVGL (embedded in the package, not an external library). It opens a
 Wayland or X11 window, or draws on a framebuffer console when asked to. It also
 offers the sermo command through update-alternatives.

Package: sermo-backend-lvgl-leger
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: sermo-backend
Conflicts: sermo-backend-lvgl
Replaces: sermo-backend-lvgl
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - LVGL backend, light build
 sermo builds native windows from an XML description, so that a shell script
 can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge. It succeeds
 gtkdialog and keeps its XML language. One hardened core parses the description
 and runs the actions; each backend draws it with one toolkit.
 .
 This package provides lvglsermo built without the ThorVG vector engine: about
 a third smaller than sermo-backend-lvgl, with the same dialogs and values, but
 SVG icons from icon themes are not shown (PNG icons are). It replaces
 sermo-backend-lvgl; install one or the other.

