Package: sermo-backend-html
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: sermo-backend
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - static HTML export backend
 sermo builds native windows from an XML description, so that a shell script
 can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge. It succeeds
 gtkdialog and keeps its XML language. One hardened core parses the description
 and runs the actions; each backend draws it with one toolkit.
 .
 This package provides htmlsermo, which writes the dialog as one standalone
 HTML page (embedded CSS, no external file, no JavaScript by default) instead
 of opening a window; a local one-shot server mode returns the entered values.
 It needs no graphics library. It also offers the sermo command through
 update-alternatives, at the lowest priority: it only answers when no windowed
 backend is installed.

Package: sermo-doc
Section: doc
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - manual and common documentation
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered. The same script runs on eight toolkits, or is written out
 as an HTML page.
 .
 This package carries the Texinfo manual ("info sermo-doc"), ready-to-use
 example scripts under /usr/share/doc/sermo-doc/examples (trade scripts,
 toolboxes, reading a PLC, home automation, drones, sound and video, network
 and hardware monitors), and the common documentation — copyright and Debian
 changelog — that the architecture independent packages of this source link to
 instead of each carrying their own copy. Those files are identical in every
 binary package, and the four packages kept for upgrades from sermo 1.x
 hold nothing else.

Package: sermo-gtkdialog
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, sermo-doc (= ${source:Version}), sermo-backend-gtk3 (>= ${source:Version})
Provides: gtkdialog
Conflicts: gtk3dialog, gtkdialog, haplo-dialog
Breaks: gtksermo (<< 2.0~)
Replaces: gtk3dialog, gtkdialog, gtksermo (<< 2.0~), haplo-dialog
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - gtkdialog command
 sermo builds native windows from an XML description, so that a shell script
 can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge. It succeeds
 gtkdialog and keeps its XML language. One hardened core parses the description
 and runs the actions; each backend draws it with one toolkit.
 .
 This package makes /usr/bin/gtkdialog a link to gtk3sermo, so that scripts
 calling gtkdialog run unchanged. It replaces the original gtkdialog and the
 gtk3dialog package, which install the same command.

