Package: sermo-source-modbus
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - read-only Modbus input
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a dialog show live values read from a Modbus PLC (TCP or
 RTU serial line), with <input modbus>tcp://host:502?registre=1</input>. It
 installs the helper that every sermo backend runs for that tag. It is
 read-only by construction: it only calls the libmodbus read functions
 (codes 1 to 4) and contains no write code.

Package: sermo-source-opcua
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - read-only OPC UA input
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a dialog show live values read from an OPC UA server, with
 <input opcua>opc.tcp://host:4840?noeud=ns=1;s=name</input>, unencrypted or
 signed and encrypted with certificates (only the server certificates given
 are trusted). It installs the helper that every sermo backend runs for that
 tag. It is read-only: it calls no write or method service.

Package: sermo-source-mqtt
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - read-only MQTT input
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a dialog show live values read from an MQTT broker (home
 automation), with <input mqtt>mqtt://host:1883?sujet=home/room/temp</input>.
 It installs the helper that every sermo backend runs for that tag. It is
 read-only: it subscribes and reads one message, and never publishes.
 Credentials are read from a file only its owner can read, never from the
 address; topic wildcards are refused. Encrypted connections (mqtts://)
 require the certificate of the trusted authority and check the server name;
 there is no "accept everything" mode.

Package: sermo-source-mavlink
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - read-only drone telemetry (MAVLink)
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a dialog show live telemetry from a drone autopilot
 (battery, position, height, armed state), with
 <input mavlink>udp://:14550?champ=tension</input>, over UDP, TCP or a serial
 radio. It is read-only: it never sends anything on the link (no command, no
 heartbeat, no stream request), and only the autopilot is listened to.

Package: sermo-cible-mqtt
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - MQTT commands (home automation)
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a button of a dialog publish one value to an MQTT topic
 (switch a light, set a thermostat), with
 <action mqtt>mqtt://host?sujet=home/lamp&valeur=on</action>. Nothing is sent
 unless the target is in an allow-list file the user or the administrator
 wrote on purpose (~/.config/sermo/cibles-mqtt, /etc/sermo/cibles-mqtt),
 with the values allowed for each topic (a closed list or a numeric range).
 Only a click can trigger it: sermo refuses it on a timer, a field or a signal.
 Without this package, sermo can read MQTT but never publish.

Package: sermo-cible-mavlink
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - drone ground settings and safety orders
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a button of a dialog set one autopilot parameter of a
 disarmed drone, or give it one safety order (return to launch, land, cut the
 motors), with <action mavlink>tcp://host:5760?ordre=rtl</action>. Nothing is
 sent unless the user or the administrator allowed it in a list written on
 purpose (~/.config/sermo/cibles-mavlink, /etc/sermo/cibles-mavlink), with a
 range for each parameter. Arming, flight modes, motor outputs, the safety
 switch and the fence are never set. Nothing is sent while another ground
 station talks to the drone; cutting the motors needs two presses within five
 seconds. A waypoint mission (Mission Planner or QGroundControl file) can be
 sent to a disarmed drone, bounded in distance and height by the list; it is
 read back from the drone before success is reported, and never started.
 Success is reported only on the drone's own confirmation.
 Without this package, sermo can read a drone but never command it.

Package: sermo-source-media
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: sermo-cible-media
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - media player state
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a dialog show the state of a sound or video player started
 by sermo-cible-media, with <input media>media://name?donnee=etat</input>:
 stopped, playing, paused or error, and on request the position and the
 duration. It is read-only: it asks the player, and never starts or commands
 it.

Package: sermo-cible-media
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, mpv
Recommends: bubblewrap
Enhances: sermo-backend-gtk3, sermo-backend-gtk4, sermo-backend-qt6, sermo-backend-fltk1, sermo-backend-efl1, sermo-backend-sdl3, sermo-backend-lvgl, sermo-backend-ncurses, sermo-backend-html
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - sound and video player
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered.
 .
 This package lets a button of a dialog play a sound or a video with mpv, and
 pause, seek, set the volume or stop it, with
 <action media>media://name?commande=lire&source=file:///path</action>.
 Sources are checked before mpv sees them (file, a camera with v4l2, http,
 https, rtsp and rtsps only; no credentials in the address). Only a fixed set
 of commands reaches the player. Network sources are played in a bubblewrap
 sandbox, and refused without it; a camera window says so while it is on,
 and nothing is recorded. The player stops when the dialog closes.

Package: sermoia-mcp
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         sermo-backend-gtk3 | sermo-backend-gtk4 | sermo-backend-qt6 | sermo-backend-fltk1 | sermo-backend-efl1 | sermo-backend-sdl3 | sermo-backend-lvgl | sermo-backend-ncurses | sermo-backend-html
Recommends: sermo-backend-qt6
Suggests: xvfb
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - MCP server to write dialogs with an AI
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered. The same script runs on eight toolkits, or is written out
 as an HTML page.
 .
 sermoia-mcp is a Model Context Protocol server (JSON-RPC on standard input
 and output, no network) that lets an AI assistant write a sermo dialog, have
 the real parser check it, see it as a PNG picture and fix it, before showing
 it to the user. Previews never run the commands of the dialog; only the
 explicit "run" tool does. It serves a catalogue of validated dialogs, job
 examples included. qt6sermo renders pictures without a display; gtk3sermo,
 gtk4sermo, fltk1sermo and lvglsermo need xvfb.

Package: sermoman-mcp
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3
Description: sermo dialog boxes for shell scripts - MCP server for the manual
 sermo opens a dialog box described in XML from a shell script, and returns the
 values entered. The same script runs on eight toolkits, or is written out
 as an HTML page.
 .
 sermoman-mcp is a read-only Model Context Protocol server (JSON-RPC on
 standard input and output, no network) that gives an AI assistant sermo's
 XML reference, guide, architecture, history and examples. It runs nothing
 and writes nothing. Written in Python, standard library only.
